INT. TELEGRAPH OFFICE - FRONTIER BANK TOWN - 1889 - DAY

Dust. Brass. A clattering key. Heat.

CLERK EZEKIEL MARSH (20s, sleeve garters) taps at the telegraph. Eyes on the paper.

COLONEL HORATIO BLAKELY (60s, white mustache, medals) paces. Cane thumping.

MADAME LIVIA SOLANO (30s, green silk, fan) fans herself by the window.

TOBY GREER (teens, newsboy cap) hovers by the door with a bundle of papers.

SHERIFF ABNER WOODS (50s, star, shotgun) leans on the counter.

MRS. PRUDENCE COLE (40s, gloves, hatbox) sits primly on the bench.

                    TELEGRAPH (V.O.)
          (clicking, then spoken by Ezekiel as he decodes)
          Train... delayed... bandits... Red Rock.

                    EZEKIEL
          Train's delayed.

                    BLAKELY
          Delayed! By whom?

                    SOLANO
          Colonel, please. The heat.

                    WOODS
          Bandits at Red Rock, Colonel.

                    TOBY
          Red Rock! That's ten miles!

                    COLE
          Young man, lower your voice.

                    BLAKELY
          I demand a horse.

                    WOODS
          Nobody's riding anywhere.

                    SOLANO
          Sheriff, my trunk is on that train.

                    EZEKIEL
          More coming. Wait.

The key chatters. Everyone leans in.

                    TELEGRAPH (V.O.)
          Hostages... demand... ransom.

Cole opens her hatbox. Inside, a derringer.

                    COLE
          Gentlemen. Madame. I believe I'll be going to Red Rock.

Woods tips his hat. Blakely sputters. Solano stops fanning. Toby whistles low.

                    EZEKIEL
          (stunned)
          Ma'am?

                    COLE
          My husband is on that train.
